{"step_index":2925,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T07:42:33Z","thinking":"**Analyzing the Core Issue**\n\nI'm now deeply analyzing Anthony's directive, seeking the core issue with laser focus. My goal is to grasp the absolute ground truth. I'm focusing on the \"Silence & Black Box\" aspect. I see files being created and edited, commands running, but there is no feedback.\n\n\n**Defining the Communication Need**\n\nI've zeroed in on the critical lack of real-time vocal feedback from the agents. They're silently executing tasks, creating a frustrating black box. The solution is the mandated \"4-Beat Mandatory Speech Hook Runtime Contract\". Agents will announce their intent, status, results, and transitions through distinct vocalizations, ensuring transparent communication during their work. I will be making the lead operations agent sound like Evan, aka `bm_george`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"bash /Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/ops/scripts/agent_speak.sh maxx \"Anthony, Maxx here. I hear you loud and clear. Closing the speech blind spot right now. Locking in the mandatory four-beat audio contract—intent before action, status during, result after, transition next. No more silent executions.\"","Cwd":"/Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain","RequestedTerminalID":"","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":8000,"toolAction":"Beat 1 Spoken Intent Dispatch for Maxx","toolSummary":"Agent speak Beat 1 Intent"}}]}
